# My Travel Guide

My Travel Guide is a small single-page website created for Homework 2. It uses a simple MVC structure to display information about travel destinations, food, and travel experiences without reloading the page.

## Features

- Home, Destinations, Food, and About views
- Button-based navigation between views
- Travel images and responsive page layout
- Styling written in Sass and compiled to CSS

## Project Structure

```text
index.html       Main HTML page
app/             Application entry point and controller
model/           Page content and view-changing logic
scss/            Sass source styles
css/             Compiled CSS
images/          Images used by the pages
```

## Getting Started

Install the development dependencies:

```bash
npm install
```

Start the local development server:

```bash
npm run serve
```

Open the local URL provided by `live-server` in a browser.

To compile the Sass stylesheet manually, run:

```bash
npx sass scss/style.scss css/style.css --no-source-map
```

## How It Works

The application starts in `app/app.js`, which loads the controller. The controller listens for clicks on the navigation buttons and requests the matching page from the model. The model then updates the `#app` element with the selected view.

